			"Message": "feat(Wind): Refactor profile config and add OS detection for workbench\n\nRefactor ResolveConfiguration to use a reusable DefaultProfile variable instead of duplicate inline profile objects. Add OS configuration with release (parsed from navigator.userAgent), hostname, and arch (arm64/x86_64 detection) required by the VS Code workbench.\n\nImprove IPCRendererShim to handle known no-op vscode: channels (createSharedProcessChannelConnection, toggleDevTools, reloadWindow, etc.) without logging warnings. Return undefined for truly unmapped channels instead of calling non-existent Tauri commands.\n\nAdd stub for utilityProcessWorker in TauriMainProcessService to prevent UtilityProcessWorkerWorkbenchService from hanging.\n\nThese changes complete workbench initialization requirements and reduce noise from expected IPC calls.",
			"SHA": "948a69b7a3621f99db02332b421eec149d216a89"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-08T21:15:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Add Electron workbench debugging checkpoints and profile URI fixes\n\nCoordinate two Land submodules to improve Electron workbench loading and fix profile configuration:\n\n- **Sky**: Add workbench.js checkpoints (WB1-WB5) to trace initialization hangs at resolveWindowConfiguration, setupNLS, import(workbenchUrl), return, and main(). Fix reviveProfile() to handle undefined location from Vite cache by injecting required URI properties (location, promptsHome, extensionsResource, mcpResource). Add desktop.main.js checkpoint logging (CP1-CP6) to trace initServices() failures. Replace 3385 static side-effect imports with sequential dynamic imports to prevent WKWebView module loader overwhelm, with progress logging every 10 modules and error recovery.\n\n- **Wind**: Add missing URI fields to default profile configuration in ResolveConfiguration - location (vscode-userdata scheme), promptsHome, extensionsResource, and mcpResource paths. These were undefined, preventing the workbench from locating user data directories. Improve TauriMainProcessService error handling with storage stub methods to prevent NativeWorkbenchStorageService hangs, return undefined on IPC failures instead of throwing, and downgrade failed channel call logs from error to warning.\n\nThese changes enable the Electron workbench to load in Tauri's WKWebView by handling module loading sequentially and fixing profile path resolution.",
			"SHA": "5591b6d4fd23a6325d29501dae8e16d720953244"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-08T16:15:06Z",
